Note: The exact console output and startup duration may differ.

## 3. Create Advertisement – POST

**API URL:**

```http
POST http://localhost:8080/api/ads
```

**Request Body:**

```json
{
  "title": "Summer Sale 2026",
  "advertiser": "ABC Company",
  "description": "Special discount campaign",
  "budget": 15000.00,
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "startDate": "2026-11-10",
  "endDate": "2026-11-30"
}
```

**Expected Response:**

```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "Summer Sale 2026",
  "advertiser": "ABC Company",
  "description": "Special discount campaign",
  "budget": 15000.00,
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "startDate": "2026-11-10",
  "endDate": "2026-11-30",
  "createdAt": "2026-11-09T14:00:00"
}
```

Expected HTTP Status: `201 Created`

The ID and timestamp are generated by the application.

## 4. View All Advertisements – GET

**API URL:**

```http
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ads
```

**Expected Response:**

```json
[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "title": "Summer Sale 2026",
    "advertiser": "ABC Company",
    "description": "Special discount campaign",
    "budget": 15000.00,
    "status": "ACTIVE",
    "startDate": "2026-11-10",
    "endDate": "2026-11-30",
    "createdAt": "2026-11-09T14:00:00"
  }
]
```

Expected HTTP Status: `200 OK`

## 5. Search Advertisement – GET by ID

**API URL:**

```http
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ads/1
```

Expected output: Returns advertisement details for ID 1.

Expected HTTP Status: `200 OK`

## 6. Update Advertisement – PUT

**API URL:**

```http
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/ads/1
```

**Request Body:**

```json
{
  "title": "Winter Sale 2026",
  "advertiser": "ABC Company",
  "description": "Updated advertising campaign",
  "budget": 20000.00,
  "status": "PAUSED",
  "startDate": "2026-11-10",
  "endDate": "2026-12-10"
}
```

Expected output: Updated advertisement information.

Expected HTTP Status: `200 OK`

## 7. Delete Advertisement – DELETE

**API URL:**

```http
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/ads/1
```

Expected HTTP Status: `204 No Content`

The advertisement is deleted from the database.

## 8. Error Output

When an advertisement ID does not exist:

```http
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ads/999
```

Expected Response:

```json
{
  "error": "Advertisement not found: 999"
}
```

Expected HTTP Status: `404 Not Found`

## 9. H2 Database Output

Open the H2 console:

```text
http://localhost:8080/h2-console
```

Connection details:

```text
JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:adspheredb
Username: sa
Password: (leave blank)
```

Database table:

```sql
SELECT * FROM ADVERTISEMENTS;
```

This displays advertisement records stored during the current application session.

